<title>AUSTRALIA: First Provincial year net profit falls.</title>
<headline>First Provincial year net profit falls.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to June 30.</p>
<p>		 (million A$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Operating profit		    3.47  vs  3.08</p>
<p>    Net				     2.11  vs  2.40</p>
<p>    Final dividend (cents)	    8.0   vs  8.0</p>
<p>    Total dividend (cents)	   17.0   vs 20.8</p>
<p>    Sales				  42.38  vs 33.24</p>
<p>    Other income			  2.18  vs  2.10</p>
<p>    Shr (cents)			  15.20  vs 22.76</p>
<p>    Abnormal items			1.49  vs  nil</p>
<p>Dividend is 100 pct franked  </p>
<p>Pay date: n/a</p>
<p>Reg date: n/a</p>
<p>    Tax			   credit  0.13  vs  0.69 expense</p>
<p>    Interest			     25.88  vs 20.49</p>
<p>    Depreciation			  1.12  vs  0.73</p>
<p>    Minorities			    nil   vs  nil</p>
<p>NOTE: Queensland-based First Provincial Building Society Ltd announced on July 31 it planned a three-way merger with Northern Building Society and Sunstate Credit Union to create First Australian Building Society.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 373 1800</p>
</text>
